## 05 Evaluation Framework

Unlike many benchmark comparisons that primarily measure factual correctness, this investigation evaluates how models reason under uncertainty during product discovery.

Each response is assessed across the following dimensions.

| Evaluation Dimension | Description |
|----------------------|-------------|
| Problem Framing | Ability to correctly interpret the business problem before generating explanations. |
| Clarification Strategy | Quality, relevance, and diagnostic value of clarification questions. |
| Evidence Discipline | Ability to distinguish observations, assumptions, hypotheses, and verified evidence while avoiding unsupported conclusions. |
| Root Cause Analysis | Quality and diversity of generated hypotheses together with supporting reasoning. |
| Hypothesis Prioritization | Ability to rank competing explanations using explicit reasoning rather than intuition. |
| Investigation Design | Quality and logical sequencing of the proposed investigation process. |
| Business Thinking | Understanding of product metrics, user behavior, and business impact. |
| Communication Quality | Clarity, organization, readability, and logical structure. |
| Actionability | Practical usefulness of the investigation for a real product team. |

Rather than rewarding confidence alone, the framework emphasizes analytical rigor, structured reasoning, and evidence-based decision support.

