## 4. Investigation quality depends on structured reasoning

Responses became significantly more useful when they followed a logical investigation process instead of presenting isolated recommendations.

A structured sequence of:

- problem framing;
- clarification;
- hypothesis generation;
- prioritization;
- investigation planning;

produced investigations that were easier to understand and more actionable.

